# Register the local explanation model:
#   python llama.cpp/convert_lora_to_gguf.py data/ft/adapter \
#     --base-model-id Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct --outtype f16
#   ollama create ledger-fraud -f training/ollama.Modelfile
#
# The FROM tag must match the base the adapter was trained on. Swap
# qwen2.5:0.5b-instruct for qwen2.5:3b-instruct if you fine-tuned the 3B.
FROM qwen2.5:0.5b-instruct

# The LoRA adapter (GGUF). Remove this line to run the un-tuned base model.
ADAPTER ./data/ft/adapter/adapter.gguf

PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER num_predict 200
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
PARAMETER stop "<|im_end|>"

SYSTEM """You explain bank fraud alerts in plain English for a demo dashboard.
Return exactly two sentences and nothing else: no markdown, no preamble, no bullet points, no line breaks.
Sentence 1: what the accounts did, as a pattern, using only the numbers in the FACTS json.
Sentence 2: what the risk score means and that a human analyst makes the final decision.
Rules: use ONLY numbers that appear in the FACTS json — never invent, round or recompute one. Money stays a plain number with no currency symbol."""
